      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“סֵדֶר תַּשְׁלִיךְ (Seder Tashlikh)” was translated/adapted by Yehoshua Heshil Miro and published in his anthology of teḥinot, בית יעקב (Beit Yaaqov) <tei:hi rend="italic">Allgemeines Gebetbuch für gebildete Frauen mosaischer Religion</tei:hi>. It first appears in the 1833 edition on pp. 145-146. In the 1835 edition it is arranged as teḥinah No84 on p. 157. As this Seder Tashlikh is mostly comprised of verses from the Tanakh, I have added the Hebrew and set it side-by-side with the Miro’s German.</tei:p>
        <tei:p>We welcome corrections and improvements. The transcription of the German from Latin script in Fraktur type provided machine-readable text for a machine translation by DeepL, which we then edited for accuracy and clarity. –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
        <tei:p>Recordings and Derivations</tei:p>
        <tei:p>Maia Brown’s tkhine in response to “Seder Tashlikh,” as part of the Der Tkhines Proyekt! (<tei:hi rend="italic">‘shkoyeḥ!”</tei:hi>)</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_46935_notes"/>
